      {
        "id": 116087,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-08-25T19:14:24.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"ironhide1\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/i/4da419/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> ironhide1:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Thematically that doesn't work for me. It's like kicking a dead horse. There's one hero still around, but I'll zap the one that's twitching on the ground instead.</p>\n<p>I'm new here, so that is an official ruling?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Yes it's official. If there is no valid target for an effect, the effect does nothing. Think of it like this, the villain has taken out all but one hero, some of those villains certainly seem like the type to start taking things less seriously if they have already gotten that far.</p>",
